      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T22:33:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: `kPermUVBox3` is `ulvec32` (32-byte aligned via `SIMD_ALIGNED(32)`), so `vmovdqa %4,%%ymm4` can be used here instead of `vmovdqu`.\n\nAlso worth noting for a follow-up: this loop issues 9 overlapping unaligned 32-byte loads (288 bytes loaded per 96 bytes of input, with 4 cache-line splits at `0x1c, 0x24, 0x38, 0x3c`) and stores 16 bytes (`%xmm0`) per iteration. We can follow up with a 16-pixel unrolled AVX2 version using 3 aligned loads (`0x00, 0x20, 0x40`) + `vpblendd` + `vpermd` + 32-byte `%ymm0` store (~1.3x-1.8x faster) as well as AVX512BW / AVX512VBMI (`vpermt2b`, ~2.1x-4.8x faster) and NEON/RVV.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "cff8d87ca3cd3cf6c68bcefdd6a0cd4ef325699b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
